1 second per test
O_DIRECT supported on this platform for open_datasync and open_sync.

Compare file sync methods using one 8kB write:
(in "wal_sync_method" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)
        open_datasync                       230.606 ops/sec    4336 usecs/op
        fdatasync                           563.524 ops/sec    1775 usecs/op
        fsync                               162.054 ops/sec    6171 usecs/op
        fsync_writethrough                              n/a
        open_sync                           163.671 ops/sec    6110 usecs/op

Compare file sync methods using two 8kB writes:
(in "wal_sync_method" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)
        open_datasync                       107.519 ops/sec    9301 usecs/op
        fdatasync                           520.841 ops/sec    1920 usecs/op
        fsync                               164.276 ops/sec    6087 usecs/op
        fsync_writethrough                              n/a
        open_sync                            81.295 ops/sec   12301 usecs/op

Compare open_sync with different write sizes:
(This is designed to compare the cost of writing 16kB in different write
open_sync sizes.)
         1 * 16kB open_sync write           161.778 ops/sec    6181 usecs/op
         2 *  8kB open_sync writes           81.959 ops/sec   12201 usecs/op
         4 *  4kB open_sync writes           40.420 ops/sec   24740 usecs/op
         8 *  2kB open_sync writes           20.128 ops/sec   49682 usecs/op
        16 *  1kB open_sync writes           10.192 ops/sec   98116 usecs/op

